{"name":"Antique Viola","hex":"#928ba6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"antique","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having existed in ancient times, descended from antiquity; used especially in reference to Greece and Rome.","Belonging to former times, not modern, out of date, old-fashioned."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In general, anything very old; specifically:\n An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance.","An old object perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/antique"},{"term":"viola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowering plants, of the genus Viola, including the violets and pansies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bowed  tenor instrument larger than a violin but smaller than a cello, used in orchestras and string quartets.","An organ stop with a similar tone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antique","blocks":[{"text":"An antique is an item perceived as having value because of its aesthetic or historical significance, and often defined as at least 100 years old, although the term is often used loosely to describe any object that is old. An antique is usually an item that is collected or desirable because of its age, beauty, rarity, condition, utility, personal emotional connection, or other unique features. It is an object that represents a previous era or time period in human history. Vintage and collectible are used to describe items that are old, but do not meet the 100-year criterion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg/330px-06_Restoration_of_gilded_mirror_in_Muzeum_Gornoslaskie%2C_Bytom%2C_Poland_-_furniture_restorer_working.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antique"},{"title":"Viola","blocks":[{"text":"The viola ( vee-OH-lə, Italian: [ˈvjɔːla, viˈɔːla]) is a string instrument of the violin family, and is usually bowed when played. The viola is slightly larger than the violin and has a lower sound. Since the 18th century, it has been the middle or alto voice of the violin family, between the violin (which is tuned a perfect fifth higher) and the cello (which is tuned an octave lower). The strings from low to high are typically tuned to C3, G3, D4, and A4."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Bratsche.jpg/330px-Bratsche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viola"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg/500px-%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg/1280px-%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg/500px-%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An antique shop in Da'an District, Taipei, Taiwan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E9%87%91%E5%B7%9D%E5%A1%A2%E8%A5%BF%E6%B4%8B%E5%8F%A4%E8%91%A3_20240111.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Kepler-world.jpg/500px-Kepler-world.jpg?utm_s